            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "## A photogrammetric mesh, drawn where it stands\n\nA **3D Tiles** tileset — the AGI headquarters in Exton, Pennsylvania, surveyed from the air — added to the map straight from its URL, with no query behind it.\n\nA tileset carries its geometry at its **real altitude**, while the map's ground sits at zero: the layer brings the mesh **down to the ground** so it stands on the satellite image instead of floating above it. The camera looks in steeply, at 69.5°.\n\n**Ctrl + drag** to rotate and tilt, scroll to zoom. To move the mesh, open the side panel with the arrow at the top left of the map, expand the layer, and look under **Position**.\n\nThe tiles stream from a public bucket and are heavy: around 300 MB of GPU memory at close range, so give them a moment on a slow connection.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
